{
 "case:accusation.methods.0": "Met Damjan in the rear vestibule during the Skopje stop, stabbed him with the cataloguing awl, took his red folio and left the train before he died inside Compartment 6.",
 "case:accusation.methods.1": "Used Emil’s emergency key after Tabanovce, killed Damjan on the lower berth and locked the compartment from the corridor.",
 "case:accusation.methods.2": "Poisoned Damjan’s tea in the dining car, then added the puncture wound after the compartment was opened at Preševo.",
 "case:accusation.methods.3": "Reached Damjan through the night window at Kumanovo and escaped across the tracks before the train departed.",
 "case:accusation.motives.0": "To stop Damjan proving that she was Mila Danevska, that Elena died in the 2011 fire, and that the stolen identity concealed the foundation transfer.",
 "case:accusation.motives.1": "To protect Nikola from losing the family’s old insurance settlement.",
 "case:accusation.motives.2": "To prevent Mara publishing criticism of the foundation’s recent charity work.",
 "case:accusation.motives.3": "To hide Emil’s bribe and avoid being fined for leaving the train at the wrong station.",
 "case:accusation.proofLabels.0": "Why the killer was never inside the locked room",
 "case:accusation.proofLabels.1": "The attack and departure at Skopje",
 "case:accusation.proofLabels.2": "The name Damjan’s report would expose",
 "case:accusation.successTitle": "The passenger list corrected",
 "case:briefing.0": "International Night Train 417 is running north through the dark toward Belgrade. Its sleeping car left Veles almost full, stopped at Skopje across midnight, called at Kumanovo and Tabanovce, and is now standing under the white border lamps at Preševo. Some passengers are asleep. Others have already stepped off into the night.",
 "case:briefing.1": "At 01:52, sleeper attendant Emil Stojanov opened Compartment 6 to return a passport and found Damjan Ristev, fifty-two, dead beside the lower berth. Damjan had a single narrow puncture wound beneath his left shoulder. There was no weapon in the room.",
 "case:briefing.2": "The compartment appeared impossible. Its sliding door was locked, the brass privacy bolt was thrown from inside and the window was latched. Border officers forced the emergency release only after Damjan failed to answer. Nothing large enough for a person connects the compartment to the corridor or the track.",
 "case:briefing.3": "Damjan was a claims investigator travelling to a civil inquiry in Belgrade. He had spent months reopening the 2011 Demir Kapija sleeper fire, in which one of two sisters died. Witnesses saw him carrying a red document folio before Skopje. The folio is missing, and the passengers disagree about whom he intended to name in his report.",
 "case:briefing.4": "Train 417 cannot remain at the border until daylight. Reconstruct the stops, decide whether the locked compartment was truly the scene of the attack, and identify which passenger left the train with a reason to silence Damjan Ristev.",
 "case:epilogue.0": "By dawn, sleeping car 218 stood empty on a siding outside Preševo. The blue berth card for Compartment 8 was still clipped beside the door, carrying Elena Danevska north after the woman using that name had stepped onto the Skopje platform.",
 "case:epilogue.1": "The Belgrade inquiry restored Elena Danevska’s name to the woman who died in the 2011 fire and reopened the forged foundation transfer. Independent trustees kept the Danevski Relief Foundation operating so that its beneficiaries did not lose help because of its director’s crimes.",
 "case:epilogue.2": "Dr. Hana Koleva filed a corrected identification and later taught the case as a warning against naming bodies from rooms, luggage or passenger lists. Petar Rusev’s father was formally cleared of causing the fire, although the railway accepted that its failed wiring had delayed the alarm.",
 "case:epilogue.3": "Emil Stojanov lost his international sleeper assignment for the bribe. His evidence still fixed the moment a passenger vanished from the record: a passport returned at 23:50, a suitcase unloaded at 00:04, and a name left behind in blue ink.",
 "case:epilogue.4": "Damjan’s report reached the inquiry in the same railway envelope he had hidden behind the berth. On its final page he had written one sentence twice: the dead deserve more than the name that is easiest to file.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.0": "The impossible room was Damjan’s refuge, not the killer’s escape.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.1": "The decisive passenger left at Skopje while the manifest said she was still aboard.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.2": "Use the accusation form: Damjan’s bolt, the platform departure and the wrong sister’s name.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.0": "The accusation needs three links: the locked room, the Skopje exit and the old identity.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.1": "Choose proof showing that Damjan locked himself in, that the attacker left at 00:06 and that the dental report threatened that passenger.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.2": "Accuse the person whose name remained on the manifest after she carried Damjan’s folio off the train.",
 "case:hints.h_archive.levels.0": "Damjan hid the conclusion, but the original records travelled separately.",
 "case:hints.h_archive.levels.1": "The 2011 identity began with a berth number and an unopened envelope.",
 "case:hints.h_archive.levels.2": "Search Damjan’s suitcase and headboard, then compare the archive box with the dental envelope.",
 "case:hints.h_bolt.levels.0": "Begin with the locked door, but do not assume the killer locked it.",
 "case:hints.h_bolt.levels.1": "Look for something only a living person inside Compartment 6 could have touched.",
 "case:hints.h_bolt.levels.2": "Examine the inside bolt and the berth call button, then answer the first board question.",
 "case:hints.h_elena.levels.0": "Elena admits leaving at Skopje, but her time protects her from the attack.",
 "case:hints.h_elena.levels.1": "The dining receipt, luggage slip and platform camera give a different sequence.",
 "case:hints.h_elena.levels.2": "Ask Elena when she left, then challenge her with the platform image.",
 "case:hints.h_identity.levels.0": "The body in 2011 was named from luggage, not from the body itself.",
 "case:hints.h_identity.levels.1": "Only one sister had the numbered porcelain crown.",
 "case:hints.h_identity.levels.2": "Compare the old berth manifest with the dental chart on the board.",
