 "case:locations.attendant_office.art.props.0.label": "Manifest desk",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.art.props.1.label": "Passport rack",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.art.props.2.label": "Luggage cage",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.art.props.3.label": "Cash pouch",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.art.props.4.label": "Archive box",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.description": "Emil’s office is a fold-down seat and desk beside Compartment 1. A locked mesh cage behind it holds checked bags and Damjan’s archive box. Passenger passports sit in numbered envelopes above the desk until the two border inspections are complete. Every alteration should be written on the international manifest in red ink.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_archive.label": "The 2011 archive folder",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_archive.text": "Damjan’s checked archive box contains the burned train’s berth list and first identification report. Elena Danevska had Berth 9; Mila Danevska had Berth 10. The body in Berth 10 was named from location and luggage, with dental comparison marked ‘pending’.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_baggage.label": "The Skopje baggage slips",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_baggage.text": "A porter’s carbon copy records one small suitcase unloaded from Compartment 8 at 00:04. Its printed destination is Belgrade. Beside it, someone has written ‘passenger ill — remove here’ without a signature.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_dental.label": "The sealed dental envelope",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_dental.text": "Inside the archive folder is an envelope stamped RECEIVED 21 NOV 2011 — AFTER CLOSURE. It contains separate dental charts for Elena and Mila, plus the post-mortem chart from the body in Berth 10.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_insurance.label": "The old insurance settlement",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_insurance.text": "The last pocket of Damjan’s archive box holds the 2012 settlement. The survivor named Elena and her brother Nikola received the family payment. Nikola’s signature acknowledges that the identification could be reopened if new medical evidence appeared.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_ledger.label": "The foundation audit",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_ledger.text": "A slim audit ledger is clipped beneath the dental envelope. It tracks a €180,000 transfer made before the 2011 fire with Elena’s forged signature, then written off after the woman named as Mila was declared dead.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_manifest.label": "The international manifest",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_manifest.text": "The working manifest matches the copy already in the case file. Nikola is marked off at Kumanovo. Elena remains blue and unaltered all the way to Belgrade. No red-ink early-departure note appears beside her name.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_passports.label": "The passport rack and cash pouch",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.hotspots.hs_attendant_passports.text": "Envelope 8 is empty and creased. A pencil note on its back says ‘returned SKP 23:50’. In Emil’s cash pouch, the shift total is exactly €100 over the receipts, folded apart from the railway money.",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.name": "The attendant’s office and luggage cage",
 "case:locations.attendant_office.summary": "The manifest desk, passport rack, baggage slips and archive box Damjan brought aboard.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.art.props.0.label": "Lower berth",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.art.props.1.label": "Sliding door",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.art.props.2.label": "Night window",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.art.props.3.label": "Washbasin",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.art.props.4.label": "Call panel",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.description": "Compartment 6 is narrow enough that the open washbasin almost touches the lower berth. Damjan’s suitcase sits beneath the window, his coat lies where the border officers cut it away, and the brass privacy bolt remains bent from the emergency release. The air smells of wool, metal and the dining car’s lemon soap.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_bolt.label": "The inside bolt",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_bolt.text": "The brass bolt is genuinely thrown into its socket. On the protected inner face, beneath the damage from the emergency release, there is a dark thumb-shaped smear that the first officers did not touch.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_call.label": "The berth call button",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_call.text": "The call button beside the berth is depressed and slow to return. Its tiny indicator is lit red, although Emil says no bell sounded in his office. A service label gives the panel’s serial number.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_coat.label": "Damjan’s coat",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_coat.text": "Damjan’s dark travelling coat has been cut open by the border medic. A single narrow hole passes through the back below the left shoulder. The lining is heavily stained, but the outer cloth shows a thinner trail running toward the hem.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_headboard.label": "The loose headboard",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_headboard.text": "One screw in the padded headboard has been loosened by hand. Behind it is a blue railway ticket envelope, flattened against the wall and sealed with Damjan’s initials.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_luggage.label": "The open suitcase",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.hotspots.hs_comp_luggage.text": "Damjan’s suitcase contains two shirts, a shaving kit and an inventory card in his handwriting. The card lists a red document folio that is no longer in the compartment. His wallet, watch and travel money remain.",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.name": "Compartment 6",
 "case:locations.compartment_six.summary": "Damjan’s locked sleeper compartment, with the body, lower berth and missing red folio.",
 "case:locations.dining_car.art.props.0.label": "Table Four",
 "case:locations.dining_car.art.props.1.label": "Service counter",
 "case:locations.dining_car.art.props.2.label": "Receipt rail",
 "case:locations.dining_car.art.props.3.label": "Journalist’s seat",
 "case:locations.dining_car.art.props.4.label": "Tea trolley",
 "case:locations.dining_car.description": "The dining car has six small tables under shaded lamps. Only tea, coffee and cold food were served after Veles. Receipts are pinned by time behind the counter, and the last passengers left when the train rolled into Skopje. Table Four still holds a folded napkin and a circle left by a tea glass.",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_notebook.label": "Mara’s notebook pouch",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_notebook.text": "Mara left a zip pouch beneath her seat. It contains an article outline, a bank-transfer receipt to Damjan and the line: ‘Do not publish the sister’s name until D.R. confirms the dental match.’",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_receipts.label": "The midnight receipts",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_receipts.text": "The numbered receipts show two teas at Table Four at 23:41, paid by Damjan. A separate receipt keeps Hana and Mara at Table Two from 23:48 until the Skopje departure announcement.",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_table.label": "Table Four",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_table.text": "Under the folded napkin is one of Damjan’s index cards. It reads: ‘E.D. — rear vestibule — five minutes when Skopje opens. Report remains sealed until 08:00.’ A diagonal red line matches the folder marks in his suitcase.",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_trolley.label": "The tea service",
 "case:locations.dining_car.hotspots.hs_dining_trolley.text": "The pot used for Damjan’s table still contains plain mountain tea. The cups were washed together, and the server saw both Damjan and Elena drink from the same pot. Nothing in the service explains a puncture wound or the blood in the vestibule.",
 "case:locations.dining_car.name": "The dining car",
 "case:locations.dining_car.summary": "A nearly empty midnight carriage where Damjan arranged his final private meeting.",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.art.props.0.label": "Platform door",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.art.props.1.label": "Corridor door",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.art.props.2.label": "Door sensor",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.art.props.3.label": "Steel handrail",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.art.props.4.label": "Radio shelf",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.description": "The rear vestibule is a ribbed steel chamber between the sleeper and the sealed luggage van. One door opens onto station platforms; the other leads back into the corridor. At speed the floor shakes and the windows show only reflected emergency lights. During a stop, it is the quietest place on the train to speak privately.",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_camera.label": "The Skopje platform image",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_camera.text": "Border police have sent a still from Skopje’s platform camera. A woman in a grey wool coat steps down from the rear sleeper door at 00:06. She carries a small suitcase and a red folio against her chest.",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_radio.label": "The station-police bulletin",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_radio.text": "A radio bulletin from Skopje reports that a cleaner found a narrow steel awl in a platform bin after Train 417 departed. The tool has a dark stain near the point and a grey wool fibre caught beneath its folding handle.",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_sensor.label": "The platform-door sensor",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_sensor.text": "The electronic latch keeps its last twenty events. The rear platform door opened one minute after the Skopje arrival and remained open for the entire service stop. It closed seconds before the train moved.",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_threshold.label": "The platform threshold",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.hotspots.hs_vestibule_threshold.text": "A dark drop sits in the ridged steel where the platform door meets the floor. A second smear marks the corridor-side handrail. Both are sheltered from rain and align with the trail leading toward Compartment 6.",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.name": "The rear vestibule",
 "case:locations.rear_vestibule.summary": "The steel platform between carriages, with the Skopje door sensor and the first trace of blood.",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.art.props.0.label": "Compartment doors",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.art.props.1.label": "Corridor runner",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.art.props.2.label": "Berth-card clips",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.art.props.3.label": "Linen cupboard",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.art.props.4.label": "Rear vestibule",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.description": "The corridor runs the length of sleeping car 218. Compartment doors line one side and black windows the other. Blue berth cards sit in brass clips beside each door. A patterned runner hides dirt well, and the rear half of the carriage has already been wiped once since Skopje.",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_cards.label": "The berth cards",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_cards.text": "Each blue card shows a passenger, destination and wake-up request. Compartment 8 still displays ELENA DANEVSKA · BELGRADE · ABOARD. Its lower edge is creased as though someone lifted it and pushed it back into the clip.",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_linen.label": "The service laundry",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_linen.text": "The linen cupboard holds sealed pillowcases and a canvas laundry sack. Inside the sack is one damp hand towel, marked with diluted rust-coloured streaks and the lemon scent used in the dining car sinks.",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_plan.label": "The carriage diagram",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_plan.text": "An evacuation diagram shows the dining-car connection at the forward end, eight compartments along the corridor, Emil’s office beside Compartment 1 and the rear vestibule seven metres beyond Compartment 6. There is no connecting door between compartments.",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_runner.label": "The patterned runner",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.hotspots.hs_corridor_runner.text": "Under oblique light, a chain of tiny brown marks appears between the rear vestibule and Compartment 6. The drops grow smaller toward the compartment. A clean rectangular gap interrupts the trail beside the linen cupboard.",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.name": "The sleeper corridor",
 "case:locations.sleeper_corridor.summary": "Eight compartments, a patterned runner, berth cards and a service-linen cupboard.",
 "case:setting": "International Night Train 417 · Skopje–Preševo · November 2027",
 "case:sketchCredit": "SKETCH: FRIDAY 12 NOVEMBER 2027 · CARRIAGE TIME",
 "case:sketchTitle": "SLEEPING CAR 218",
