 "case:timeline.prompt": "Put the last journey of Compartment 6 in order. All times use the clock displayed inside sleeping car 218.",
 "case:timeline.title": "The night train, reconstructed",
 "case:title": "The Midnight Express",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_departure.insight": "Elena says she left before midnight, but she was still sharing tea with Damjan at 23:41, her suitcase was removed at 00:04 and the platform camera records her exit at 00:06.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_departure.response.0": "I was not watching the station clock. I meant that I decided to leave before midnight.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_departure.response.1": "You left at 00:06, after the vestibule meeting and one minute after Damjan pressed his call button.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_departure.response.2": "Then the difference is twelve minutes, not a murder. I was ill and trying to get off before the train moved.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_departure.response.3": "Elena’s safe early departure has moved into the exact window in which Damjan was wounded and returned to his compartment.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_departure.title": "Six minutes after midnight",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_folio.insight": "Damjan’s inventory, the red transfer on his meeting card and the folio’s brass corner in the platform image identify the folder Elena carried as Damjan’s.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_folio.response.0": "Red leather folders are not unique. The foundation has used them for years.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_folio.response.1": "Damjan listed his folio when he boarded. It disappeared from a locked room, and the one under your arm has its diagonal scuff and brass corner.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_folio.response.2": "He gave me papers in the dining car. I took them because they concerned my family. I did not kill him for them.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_folio.response.3": "Elena no longer denies taking Damjan’s papers. She now disputes only what happened before she carried them onto the platform.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_folio.title": "The folio under her arm",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_emil_manifest.insight": "Emil returned Elena’s passport, accepted her money and handled her berth card without turning it white. His manifest kept her aboard after she left.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_emil_manifest.response.0": "She said she was ill. I thought I could correct the manifest after the porters finished.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_emil_manifest.response.1": "You took €100, gave her the document she needed to leave the station and pushed her berth card back into the aboard position.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_emil_manifest.response.2": "Yes. I hid an early departure. I did not know she had Damjan’s folio or that he was bleeding seven metres away.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_emil_manifest.response.3": "Emil’s bribe explains how the passenger list disagreed with the train. It does not explain the blood in the rear vestibule.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_emil_manifest.title": "A passenger left aboard on paper",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hana_identification.insight": "The 2011 form marked dental comparison as pending. The unopened charts arrived after closure and directly contradict the name Hana signed.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hana_identification.response.0": "I confirmed the teeth described in the post-mortem chart, not a comparison with the sisters’ original records. I chose my words badly.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hana_identification.response.1": "You signed a named identification while the only medical comparison was still missing.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hana_identification.response.2": "Yes. The berth, luggage and passport had already become the identity, and I allowed the form to make that look scientific.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hana_identification.response.3": "Hana admits the professional failure. Her new comparison corrects it and points away from her own name.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hana_identification.title": "Pending was never completed",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mara_work.insight": "Mara transferred Damjan €2,400 for research and planned an article around the dental evidence.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mara_work.response.0": "I paid expenses, not a bounty for a particular conclusion. Sources do not digitise archives for free.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mara_work.response.1": "You concealed a formal commission and a publication plan built around Damjan’s report.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mara_work.response.2": "Because buying research sounds worse than doing it. I still sat with Hana until the train left Skopje.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mara_work.response.3": "Mara had a professional stake in the missing report, but her lie is about ownership of the story rather than access to the vestibule.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mara_work.title": "A commissioned investigation",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_money.insight": "The transfer was disputed as a forgery before the fire, and the later settlement let the surviving family assign it to the sister declared dead.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_money.response.0": "The supplier returned part of the money. I was trying to keep a small charity from collapsing after a funeral.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_money.response.1": "You signed a settlement that allowed the identity to be reopened, then treated the transfer as Mila’s crime because Mila was the name on the grave.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_money.response.2": "I suspected something was wrong. I never knew enough to accuse the sister who survived.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_money.response.3": "Nikola protected the family’s money and avoided the identity question, but his silence does not place him at the Skopje rear door.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_money.title": "The dead sister carried the debt",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_petar_lock.insight": "Damjan’s blood is on the protected bolt face, his call was pressed at 00:05 and his blood trail ends at the door. The bent socket came from the later emergency opening.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_petar_lock.response.0": "Then the sticking socket is irrelevant. Damjan locked it himself.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_petar_lock.response.1": "He was already wounded, entered Compartment 6 and called for help. The killer never needed to leave that room.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_petar_lock.response.2": "Which means the key register is noise. You need the place where the blood trail begins.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_petar_lock.response.3": "Petar’s mechanical theory collapses, but his correction turns the impossible room into Damjan’s final refuge.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_petar_lock.title": "The lock was Damjan’s choice",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.conclusion": "Damjan was punctured through the back of his coat while upright. His blood begins at the rear platform threshold and decreases toward Compartment 6. He was attacked in the rear vestibule, pressed cloth to the wound and walked seven metres back to the room he could lock.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.options.0": "On the lower berth inside Compartment 6",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.options.1": "At Table Four in the dining car",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.options.2": "In the rear vestibule beside the platform door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.options.3": "On the Kumanovo platform after leaving the train",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.proofLabels.0": "The wound before the room",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.proofLabels.1": "The direction of the trail",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.question": "Where was Damjan attacked?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_attack.title": "Seven metres of corridor",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.conclusion": "Damjan’s blood and left-thumb print are protected inside the bolt, and his berth call was pressed at 00:05. He was alive after the puncture wound, entered Compartment 6, locked the door and tried to summon help. The locked room contains the victim’s last action, not the killer’s escape trick.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.options.0": "The killer used a duplicate key and bent the bolt from the corridor",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.options.1": "Damjan was alive after he was wounded, entered Compartment 6 and bolted it himself",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.options.2": "Someone escaped through the ventilation gap above the night window",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.options.3": "Border officers accidentally created the blood mark while forcing the door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.proofLabels.0": "Who moved the bolt",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.proofLabels.1": "What happened after the wound",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.question": "What does the locked compartment actually prove?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_bolt.title": "The bolt was a refuge",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.conclusion": "The body recovered from Mila’s assigned berth carried Elena’s uniquely numbered crown. Elena died in 2011. Mila survived with Elena’s passport and continued under her older sister’s name. The passenger record preserved the wrong identity for sixteen years.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.options.0": "Mila died in Berth 10 exactly as the luggage record says",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.options.1": "Neither sister was on the train when the fire began",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.options.2": "Elena died in Berth 10 and Mila survived under Elena’s name",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.options.3": "Nikola changed both dental charts after the insurance settlement",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.proofLabels.0": "The name assigned by the berth",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.proofLabels.1": "The identity recorded by the body",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.question": "What do the 2011 medical records establish?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_identity.title": "The wrong sister",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.conclusion": "Damjan’s report did more than rename the dead. It showed that Mila forged a €180,000 transfer, then survived as Elena and assigned the fraud to the sister declared dead. Correcting the identification would expose sixteen years of false signatures, control of the foundation and the old insurance settlement.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.options.0": "It accused Elena of causing the electrical fire with the carriage call button",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.options.1": "It linked the reversed identity to a forged foundation transfer blamed on the sister declared dead",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.options.2": "It required Nikola to surrender every building owned by the foundation",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.options.3": "It proved Mara had invented the Demir Kapija fire for her article",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.proofLabels.0": "The identity Damjan would correct",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.proofLabels.1": "What the false identity concealed",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.question": "Why did Damjan’s report threaten the survivor’s life as Elena?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_report.title": "The report behind the berth",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.conclusion": "The rear platform door was open only at Skopje, from 23:47 to 00:07. Damjan was wounded there, called from his room at 00:05 and Elena stepped off with the red folio at 00:06. The train moved at 00:08, closing the attack and escape window.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.options.0": "Veles, before Damjan entered the dining car",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.options.1": "Skopje, while the rear door stayed open across midnight",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.options.2": "Kumanovo, using the forward passenger door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.options.3": "Preševo, after border police opened Compartment 6",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.proofLabels.0": "The open rear door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.proofLabels.1": "The person who used it",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.question": "Which stop gave the attacker both the vestibule and a way off the train?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_stop.title": "The Skopje window",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.conclusion": "The woman known as Elena prepared an unrecorded Skopje departure, met Damjan in the rear vestibule and carried his folio off the train at 00:06. Damjan’s report would prove that she was Mila and expose the fraud hidden by that identity. Her person left the train; Elena’s name remained clipped beside Compartment 8.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.0": "Nikola Danevski",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.1": "Dr. Hana Koleva",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.2": "Elena Danevska",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.3": "Emil Stojanov",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.proofLabels.0": "The passenger who left at 00:06",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.proofLabels.1": "The person whose name the report would undo",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.question": "Who connects the Skopje attack to the identity Damjan was about to expose?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.title": "A name left on the train",
 "dialogues:statements.st_elena_departure.text": "Elena says she stepped off at Skopje before midnight, before Damjan went to the rear of the train.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_elena_fire.text": "Elena says Mila occupied Berth 10 and died there during the 2011 fire.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_elena_folio.text": "The red folio Elena carried from the train belonged to the foundation, not to Damjan.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_emil_call.text": "The call from Compartment 6 failed because the forward bell wire was already broken.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_emil_luggage.text": "Emil returned Elena’s passport and let her suitcase be unloaded after accepting money to delay the paperwork.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_emil_manifest.text": "Emil says no Belgrade passenger left at Skopje and Elena’s blue berth card proves she remained aboard.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hana_alibi.text": "Hana remained with Mara in the dining car from the Skopje arrival until the departure call.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hana_identification.text": "Hana says she personally confirmed the available dental identification before signing the 2011 form.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_mara_alibi.text": "Mara saw Damjan leave the dining car first and Elena follow him toward the sleeper.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_mara_work.text": "Mara says she did not hire Damjan or pay for the Demir Kapija investigation.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_nikola_money.text": "Nikola says the €180,000 transfer was a supplier advance and neither sister benefited from it.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_nikola_sister.text": "After the fire, the surviving sister changed from writing left-handed to writing right-handed.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_petar_archive.text": "Petar found the sealed dental envelope and gave it to Damjan so the old identification could be corrected.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_petar_lock.text": "Petar believes an emergency key and a sticking socket could make the door appear bolted after a killer left.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_departure.lines.0": "Elena, your ticket runs to Belgrade. Why did you leave at Skopje?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_departure.lines.1": "Damjan used the dining car to accuse me of lying about my own sister’s death. I became short of breath and decided I could not spend another night inside a sleeper.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_departure.lines.2": "Emil returned my passport and a porter found my suitcase. I stepped off before midnight, before Damjan went anywhere near the rear of the train.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_departure.lines.3": "I did not hide the fact that I left. The railway failed to update its own paper.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_departure.prompt": "When did you leave the train?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_fire.lines.0": "What do you remember about the night your sister died near Demir Kapija?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_fire.lines.1": "Smoke, metal and someone striking the corridor window with a shoe. Mila had Berth 10. I found the service door and woke up outside without my coat.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_fire.lines.2": "They gave me her damaged luggage tag in a paper bag and told me not to look at the body. Nikola identified our things.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_fire.lines.3": "Damjan signed the name sixteen years ago. If he had doubts, he should have carried them then instead of putting them on me now.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_fire.prompt": "Tell me about the 2011 fire.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_folio.lines.0": "The platform camera shows a red folio under your arm. Damjan’s red folio is missing.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_folio.lines.1": "The foundation uses red folders for donor accounts. I brought one onto the train and carried the same one off.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_folio.lines.2": "Damjan waved his own papers at me in the dining car. I never touched them.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_folio.lines.3": "A colour in a grainy photograph is not ownership.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_elena_folio.prompt": "What were you carrying on the platform?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_call.lines.0": "Compartment 6 pressed its call at 00:05. Why did you not answer?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_call.lines.1": "Because the forward bell wire was open. Compartment 7 tested it before Veles and I entered the fault in the book. The local light works even when my bell does not.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_call.lines.2": "At 00:05 I was resetting the panel beside Compartment 1. The rear platform and Compartment 6 are the length of the carriage away.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_call.lines.3": "If I had heard the bell, Damjan might be alive. That is the failure I will carry, whether or not it was my wire to repair.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_call.prompt": "Why did Damjan’s call not ring?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_luggage.lines.0": "The porter unloaded Elena’s suitcase at 00:04. Who authorised it?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_luggage.lines.1": "Elena said she was ill and might leave. She asked for her passport, then offered money so I would not delay the border sheet.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_luggage.lines.2": "I told myself I would correct the manifest after departure. Then Kumanovo arrived, then the border officers, and I left her card blue.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_luggage.lines.3": "I never saw the red folio. I was at the forward door. The rear porter moved the suitcase.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_luggage.prompt": "Who unloaded Compartment 8’s suitcase?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_manifest.lines.0": "Your manifest says Elena is still aboard. Did she leave at Skopje?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_manifest.lines.1": "No Belgrade passenger left my car without being crossed off. Nikola was the only scheduled departure before the border, and I turned his card at Kumanovo.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_manifest.lines.2": "The porters moved bags at Skopje, but passengers used the forward door where I could see them. The rear door was for luggage.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_manifest.lines.3": "If Elena appears outside, she must have returned before departure. Her blue card proves she remained aboard.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_emil_manifest.prompt": "Did anyone leave unexpectedly?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_identification.lines.0": "Your signature appears on the identification of the woman from Berth 10. What did you compare?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_identification.lines.1": "The berth assignment, a damaged luggage tag and the survivor’s passport. The body was badly burned and the family wanted a name before the funeral.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_identification.lines.2": "I personally confirmed the dental identification available to us. There was no contradiction in the file when I signed it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_identification.lines.3": "If an envelope arrived after closure, it should have been routed back to me. It was not.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_identification.prompt": "How was the body identified in 2011?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_night.lines.0": "Where were you from the Skopje arrival until the train departed?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_night.lines.1": "At Table Two with Mara. She wanted me to explain every line of a provisional dental form without letting me see the article she had already written.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_night.lines.2": "I heard the arrival announcement, the platform porters and then the departure call. I never went to the sleeper’s rear vestibule.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_night.lines.3": "My career is attached to the old mistake. Correcting it was the only useful thing I could still do.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hana_night.prompt": "Where were you during the Skopje stop?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_night.lines.0": "What happened in the dining car before Damjan disappeared?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_night.lines.1": "Damjan sat with Elena at Table Four. She kept both hands around her tea while he spoke. He showed her a red folio but did not open it flat.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_night.lines.2": "When Skopje was announced, Damjan left toward the sleeper. Elena waited perhaps a minute, then followed.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_night.lines.3": "Hana and I stayed until the departure call. She was angry with me, which made her very easy to remember.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_night.prompt": "What did you see before Skopje?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_work.lines.0": "You and Damjan were on the same overnight train to the same inquiry. Was that arranged?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_work.lines.1": "We knew each other professionally. I heard he was reopening the fire and booked the train because the route mattered to my article.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_work.lines.2": "I did not hire him, buy documents or promise payment for a name. We shared information when it suited both of us.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_work.lines.3": "His report would have helped, but a dead source is the worst possible source.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mara_work.prompt": "Why were you travelling with Damjan?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_money.lines.0": "The audit shows a €180,000 transfer before your sisters boarded the train.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_money.lines.1": "It was a supplier advance, not theft. The account was frozen after the fire and most of it was recovered.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_money.lines.2": "Damjan kept calling it motive because an ugly word makes old paperwork sound alive. Neither sister gained from that transfer.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_money.lines.3": "The insurance settlement paid for treatment and a funeral. There was no secret fortune to protect.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_money.prompt": "Was foundation money missing before the fire?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_sister.lines.0": "When you saw your surviving sister after the fire, did anything trouble you?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_sister.lines.1": "Everything troubled me. Her hair was burned, her hands were bandaged and she could not sleep without a light.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_sister.lines.2": "Elena had always written with her left hand. After the fire she used her right and said the burns had changed it. I accepted that because the alternative was unthinkable.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_sister.lines.3": "I signed what the investigators placed in front of me. I chose the sister who was breathing.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_nikola_sister.prompt": "Did the survivor seem different?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_archive.lines.0": "You found the dental envelope. What were you looking for?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_archive.lines.1": "The wiring appendix. My father was blamed for losing minutes during the evacuation, but the carriage alarm was dead before smoke reached him.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_archive.lines.2": "The dental envelope was still sealed behind the report. I gave it to Damjan because he had signed the original claim and because I wanted both errors corrected together.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_archive.lines.3": "He warned me that a corrected name could hurt living people. I told him the wrong name had already hurt the dead.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_archive.prompt": "Why did you reopen the old archive?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_lock.lines.0": "You know this model of sleeper. Can someone set the privacy bolt from the corridor?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_lock.lines.1": "Not with the door closed. But an attendant’s emergency key can hold the latch while the door appears bolted. Old sockets stick after a hard slide.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_lock.lines.2": "My first thought was that someone killed Damjan in the compartment, left with a key and let the bent socket imitate the inside bolt.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_lock.lines.3": "If there is blood on the bolt, it could have transferred when the officers forced it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_petar_lock.prompt": "How could the compartment be locked?",
 "evidence:evidence.attendant_statement.detail": "Statement by Emil Stojanov, sleeper attendant.\n\n‘I collected the Belgrade passengers’ passports after Veles and kept them in the numbered rack. At Skopje I worked the forward door while porters handled the rear. Anyone leaving early had to tell me, and I wrote every change on the manifest.\n\n‘Damjan did not ask for a wake-up. I passed Compartment 6 after Kumanovo and saw the red occupied light. At Preševo I knocked to return his passport. The privacy bolt was on and he did not answer, so I called border police and used the emergency release. Nobody had reported a call from his berth.’",
 "evidence:evidence.attendant_statement.name": "Emil’s first statement",
 "evidence:evidence.attendant_statement.summary": "Emil says no passenger left unexpectedly and that he found Damjan when returning passports at 01:52.",
 "evidence:evidence.awl_recovery.detail": "Skopje station police recovery report, 02:11.\n\nA folding steel cataloguing awl was found beneath paper cups in the bin opposite sleeping car 218. Damjan used the tool to lift old staples and wax seals; its serial number appears in a photograph of his open red folio.\n\nThe point carries Damjan’s blood. The handle was wiped, but a short grey wool fibre with a burgundy thread remains beneath the hinge. The fibre is consistent with the coat Elena wears in the 00:06 platform image.",
 "evidence:evidence.awl_recovery.name": "The recovered cataloguing awl",
 "evidence:evidence.awl_recovery.summary": "A narrow awl from Damjan’s folio was discarded in a Skopje platform bin with his blood on its point.",
 "evidence:evidence.baggage_receipt.detail": "Carbon copy from the Skopje night porter.\n\nCar 218 · Compartment 8 · one grey wheeled suitcase\nPrinted destination: BELGRADE\nRemoved: SKOPJE · 00:04\nHandwritten reason: ‘passenger ill — remove here’\nAuthorising signature: blank\n\nThe porter remembers a woman in a grey coat waiting near the rear door and an attendant saying the paperwork would be corrected later. The manifest was never corrected.",
 "evidence:evidence.baggage_receipt.name": "The Skopje baggage slip",
 "evidence:evidence.baggage_receipt.summary": "Elena’s suitcase was unloaded at 00:04 despite carrying a printed Belgrade destination tag.",
 "evidence:evidence.berth_cards.detail": "Sleeping-car berth cards are blue while a passenger is aboard and turned white when the berth becomes vacant.\n\nCompartment 5 · NIKOLA DANEVSKI · KUMANOVO · card turned white and time-stamped 00:44.\nCompartment 8 · ELENA DANEVSKA · BELGRADE · card still blue.\n\nThe lower edge of Elena’s card has a fresh diagonal crease and a graphite thumb mark matching Emil’s manifest pencil. Someone handled the card at Skopje, then pushed it back into the blue aboard position instead of recording an early departure.",
 "evidence:evidence.berth_cards.name": "The blue berth cards",
 "evidence:evidence.berth_cards.summary": "Elena’s card remains in the aboard position even though its edge was lifted during the Skopje stop.",
 "evidence:evidence.berth_manifest.detail": "Sleeping car 218 · compartments occupied after Veles.\n\n2 · Dr. Hana Koleva · Belgrade · aboard\n3 · Mara Petreska · Belgrade · aboard\n4 · Petar Rusev · Belgrade · aboard\n5 · Nikola Danevski · Kumanovo · off 00:44\n6 · Damjan Ristev · Belgrade · aboard\n8 · Elena Danevska · Belgrade · aboard\n\nInternational procedure requires an early departure to be crossed through in red ink and reported at the next border. Elena’s line has no alteration. Her blue berth card and Belgrade wake-up request remain active.",
 "evidence:evidence.berth_manifest.name": "The sleeping-car manifest",
 "evidence:evidence.berth_manifest.summary": "Elena is still marked aboard to Belgrade, while Nikola is correctly marked off at Kumanovo.",
 "evidence:evidence.call_panel_log.detail": "Service readout from call panel 218-6.\n\n00:05:18 · COMP 6 CALL SWITCH CLOSED\n00:05:18 · FORWARD BELL CIRCUIT OPEN · SIGNAL NOT DELIVERED\n\nA wire fault had been entered in the carriage maintenance book at 22:58 after Compartment 7 tested its button. Emil reset the forward panel between 23:59 and 00:07 but did not repair the wire. The local red indicator in Compartment 6 remained lit.\n\nOnly a hand inside Compartment 6 could press this button. Damjan was alive and attempting to summon help at 00:05.",
 "evidence:evidence.call_panel_log.name": "The failed berth call",
 "evidence:evidence.call_panel_log.summary": "Compartment 6 pressed its call button at 00:05, but a broken carriage wire kept the bell from reaching Emil.",
 "evidence:evidence.carriage_plan.detail": "Emergency diagram for sleeping car 218.\n\nForward end: dining-car connection, attendant office, Compartments 1–4.\nMid-car: Compartments 5–8 and service-linen cupboard.\nRear end: steel vestibule and platform door, followed by a sealed luggage van.\n\nCompartment 6 is seven metres from the rear vestibule. The night window opens only eight centimetres for ventilation. There are no connecting compartment doors, maintenance hatches large enough for a person or roof access points. The corridor is the only human route between the compartment and vestibule.",
 "evidence:evidence.carriage_plan.name": "The sleeping-car plan",
 "evidence:evidence.carriage_plan.summary": "Compartment 6 is seven metres from the rear vestibule and has no route except the corridor.",
 "evidence:evidence.cash_count.detail": "Cash reconciliation from Emil’s office.\n\nRailway sales and supplements: €286\nCash in official wallet: €286\nCash in private pouch: one €100 note, folded twice\n\nThe note carries Elena’s right-thumb print and Emil’s left-thumb print. Emil initially described it as a tip from a group that left at Veles, but no group in his car bought a supplement or signed a tip receipt. The money explains why an early departure was hidden rather than properly entered.",
 "evidence:evidence.cash_count.name": "The unexplained €100",
 "evidence:evidence.cash_count.summary": "Emil’s shift cash is €100 over the documented railway receipts, folded apart in his private pouch.",
 "evidence:evidence.coat_damage.detail": "The travelling coat has one narrow puncture below the left shoulder blade. The fibres are driven inward, consistent with an attack from behind or over Damjan’s left shoulder. There is no corresponding cut in the lower-berth upholstery.\n\nBlood soaked the inner lining around the wound, then formed a thinner downward run toward the left hem. Small transfer marks on the left cuff match the pressure of holding a folded cloth against the injury. The pattern is consistent with Damjan remaining upright and moving for several minutes before lying down.",
 "evidence:evidence.coat_damage.name": "Damjan’s damaged coat",
 "evidence:evidence.coat_damage.summary": "The wound passed through Damjan’s coat from behind, and the blood pattern shows that he walked afterward.",
 "evidence:evidence.corridor_trace.detail": "Oblique-light examination of the sleeper runner.\n\nTwelve tiny drops and two left-cuff transfers contain Damjan’s blood. The largest drop lies nearest the rear vestibule. The drops become smaller and farther apart toward Compartment 6, ending at its door track. No matching trail continues forward toward the dining car.\n\nA clean rectangular interruption beside the linen cupboard contains moisture and lemon soap. The direction of travel is from the rear vestibule to Damjan’s compartment.",
 "evidence:evidence.corridor_trace.name": "The corridor blood trace",
 "evidence:evidence.corridor_trace.summary": "Small blood drops run from the rear vestibule toward Compartment 6 and decrease as they approach the door.",
 "evidence:evidence.dental_chart.detail": "Three records compared by Dr. Hana Koleva in October 2027.\n\nElena Danevska, 2009: porcelain crown on lower left molar, laboratory number PK-4417, secured with a short gold retaining pin.\nMila Danevska, 2010: natural lower left molar, no crown and no gold dental work.\nBody from Berth 10: porcelain crown on lower left molar, PK-4417 visible beneath heat damage, with gold retaining pin intact.\n\nLaboratory number PK-4417 was made for Elena. The body identified as Mila was Elena. The person who survived the fire under Elena’s name was Mila.",
 "evidence:evidence.dental_chart.name": "The sisters’ dental records",
 "evidence:evidence.dental_chart.summary": "The dead woman had Elena’s uniquely numbered crown; Mila’s chart shows that tooth had never been treated.",
 "evidence:evidence.dining_receipts.detail": "Last service receipts before the border.\n\n23:41 · Table 4 · two mountain teas · paid D. Ristev\n23:48 · Table 2 · coffee, mineral water, cheese plate · paid M. Petreska\n00:07 · Table 2 closed by server after departure announcement\n\nThe server remembers Damjan and Elena speaking quietly until the Skopje arrival. Elena asked which sleeper door would open beside the south exit. Hana and Mara remained at Table 2, arguing over the wording of the old identification form, until the departure announcement.",
 "evidence:evidence.dining_receipts.name": "The dining-car receipts",
 "evidence:evidence.dining_receipts.summary": "Damjan and Elena shared tea at 23:41, while Hana and Mara remained together until the Skopje departure call.",
 "evidence:evidence.door_log.detail": "Automatic latch events, rear door, sleeping car 218.\n\n23:47:03 · opened · SKOPJE platform side\n23:50:11 · luggage interlock released\n00:04:26 · luggage interlock secured\n00:07:31 · closed\n00:08:04 · traction enabled\n\nThe door did not open at Kumanovo because that station used the forward sleeper door. It remained locked at Tabanovce and Preševo until border police arrived. The rear vestibule offered an exit only during the twenty-minute Skopje window.",
 "evidence:evidence.door_log.name": "The rear platform-door log",
 "evidence:evidence.door_log.summary": "The rear sleeper door stayed open from 23:47 until 00:07 during the Skopje stop.",
 "evidence:evidence.foundation_ledger.detail": "Danevski Relief Foundation audit file, January–March 2011.\n\n28 January · €180,000 transferred to North Bridge Supplies using Elena Danevska’s authorisation.\n31 January · Elena disputes the signature and schedules a meeting with foundation counsel in Belgrade.\n4 February · Elena and Mila board Night Service 312.\n11 February · surviving director ‘Elena’ states that Mila forged the transfer and died in the fire.\n\nA handwriting review matches the transfer signature to Mila’s school and bank forms. North Bridge Supplies was controlled by Mila’s boyfriend. The identity error turned the suspected forger into the dead sister and placed the foundation in the survivor’s control.",
 "evidence:evidence.foundation_ledger.name": "The foundation transfer ledger",
 "evidence:evidence.foundation_ledger.summary": "Before the fire, Mila forged Elena’s signature to divert €180,000 and the loss was later assigned to the sister declared dead.",
 "evidence:evidence.inside_bolt.detail": "Forensic examination of the Compartment 6 door.\n\nThe brass privacy bolt was fully seated before officers bent its socket with the emergency release. The outer edge carries fresh tool marks from that opening. The protected inner face carries a partial left-thumb print in Damjan Ristev’s blood. The smear runs in the direction used to push the bolt closed.\n\nNo thread, wire or foreign fibre is caught in the mechanism. The bolt could not be reached from the corridor once the sliding door was shut. Someone alive inside the compartment engaged it after Damjan began bleeding.",
 "evidence:evidence.inside_bolt.name": "The bloody inside bolt",
 "evidence:evidence.inside_bolt.summary": "Damjan’s own blood and left-thumb print are on the protected inner face of the privacy bolt.",
 "evidence:evidence.insurance_record.detail": "Final settlement following the Demir Kapija fire.\n\nBeneficiaries: Elena Danevska, survivor; Nikola Danevski, next of kin.\nPayment: family loss, medical treatment and destroyed luggage.\nSpecial clause: ‘Identification remains subject to correction if original medical evidence becomes available.’\n\nNikola signed beneath the clause. A handwritten note from Damjan says Nikola asked whether a later correction would require repayment. The record gives Nikola a reason to fear the inquiry, but it also confirms his declared Kumanovo ticket and contains no connection to the Skopje platform exit.",
 "evidence:evidence.insurance_record.name": "The 2012 insurance settlement",
 "evidence:evidence.insurance_record.summary": "The survivor and Nikola received the family settlement under an agreement that allowed the identification to be reopened.",
 "evidence:evidence.linen_towel.detail": "A white hand towel recovered from the sleeper’s laundry sack.\n\nThe diluted brown streaks contain Damjan’s blood. The damp edge contains the same lemon soap used at the dining-car sink. A porter initialled the laundry slip at 00:14 and later said he wiped what looked like spilled red wine beside Compartment 7 shortly after the Skopje departure.\n\nThe towel did not create the trail. It removed one short section of a trail already leading from the rear of the car toward Compartment 6.",
 "evidence:evidence.linen_towel.name": "The service towel",
 "evidence:evidence.linen_towel.summary": "A towel in the service laundry carries Damjan’s blood and explains the wiped section of corridor.",
 "evidence:evidence.mara_notes.detail": "Notebook and bank receipt from Mara Petreska’s pouch.\n\nTransfer: €2,400 to Damjan Ristev · research expenses · 3 August 2027.\nArticle outline: ‘The Woman Who Left Berth 10.’\nNotes: ‘Passenger list says one sister. Teeth may say the other. Do not publish name until D.R. confirms. H.K. admits the 2011 chart was provisional.’\n\nMara concealed a formal working relationship, not a chance conversation. Her dining receipt and Hana’s account place her at Table Two when Damjan went to the rear vestibule.",
 "evidence:evidence.mara_notes.name": "Mara’s commission notebook",
 "evidence:evidence.mara_notes.summary": "Mara funded Damjan’s research and planned to publish the identity question after he confirmed the dental evidence.",
 "evidence:evidence.meeting_note.detail": "Index card recovered beneath the napkin at Table Four.\n\n‘E.D. — rear vestibule — five minutes when Skopje opens.\nNo bargain. Report remains sealed until 08:00.\nAsk again about transfer authorisation and Mila’s dental envelope.’\n\nA diagonal red mark along the card’s edge matches the dyed leather of Damjan’s missing folio. The note places his planned private meeting at the same end of the carriage where his blood trail begins.",
 "evidence:evidence.meeting_note.name": "Damjan’s meeting card",
 "evidence:evidence.meeting_note.summary": "Damjan arranged to meet ‘E.D.’ in the rear vestibule for five minutes during the Skopje stop.",
 "evidence:evidence.missing_folio.detail": "Damjan’s handwritten inventory, signed when he boarded at Gevgelija.\n\nLeather suitcase · 9.4 kg\nArchive box · checked cage · seal DR-17\nRed document folio · hand carried\nBlue railway envelope · private\n\nThe suitcase, archive box and personal effects are present. The red folio is missing. A diagonal red transfer mark on an index card in the dining car matches the dyed leather. Damjan’s cash, cards and watch were not taken, making the folio a more likely target than robbery.",
 "evidence:evidence.missing_folio.name": "The missing red folio",
 "evidence:evidence.missing_folio.summary": "Damjan’s luggage inventory lists a red document folio that is absent from the locked compartment.",
 "evidence:evidence.old_manifest.detail": "Night Service 312 · 4 February 2011 · sleeping car after the Demir Kapija fire.\n\nBerth 9 · Elena Danevska · age 27 · listed survivor\nBerth 10 · Mila Danevska · age 19 · listed deceased\n\nFirst identification note: ‘Female body recovered from Berth 10. Damaged luggage tag M. DANEVSKA. Survivor presents Elena Danevska passport. Identity accepted pending dental comparison.’\n\nThe final line was never completed. A wiring appendix says the carriage alarm circuit failed before smoke reached the corridor, clearing the attendant of causing the fire but not of the delayed evacuation.",
 "evidence:evidence.old_manifest.name": "The 2011 fire manifest",
 "evidence:evidence.old_manifest.summary": "Elena had Berth 9 and Mila Berth 10, but the body in Berth 10 was identified before dental records arrived.",
 "evidence:evidence.overnight_timetable.detail": "International Night Train 417, Friday 12 November 2027. All entries use the clock displayed inside the carriage.\n\nGevgelija · 22:31\nVeles · 23:17\nSkopje · arrive 23:46 · depart 00:08\nKumanovo · arrive 00:42 · depart 00:45\nTabanovce border · arrive 01:07 · depart 01:24\nPreševo border · arrive 01:36 · scheduled depart 01:55\nVranje · 02:31\nBelgrade · 06:48\n\nSkopje was the only stop long enough for routine luggage unloading. Damjan was found at 01:52 while passports were being returned at Preševo.",
 "evidence:evidence.overnight_timetable.name": "The overnight timetable",
 "evidence:evidence.overnight_timetable.summary": "Train 417 stood at Skopje for twenty-two minutes across midnight before continuing to the border.",
 "evidence:evidence.passport_envelope.detail": "Sleeper passport envelope 8 · ELENA DANEVSKA · BELGRADE.\n\nThe envelope is empty. On the back, Emil wrote in pencil: ‘returned SKP 23:50 — passenger request.’ The international manifest contains no matching early-departure entry. Other Belgrade passports remained sealed in the rack until Preševo.\n\nElena could not lawfully cross the station exit without her passport. Emil prepared her departure before Damjan’s vestibule meeting began.",
 "evidence:evidence.passport_envelope.name": "Elena’s empty passport envelope",
 "evidence:evidence.passport_envelope.summary": "Emil returned Elena’s passport at 23:50, sixteen minutes before the platform camera recorded her departure.",
 "evidence:evidence.platform_image.detail": "Still frames from Platform Camera 4, synchronised to the station clock.\n\n00:05:54 · Elena Danevska appears in the rear doorway wearing a grey wool coat.\n00:06:02 · she steps onto the platform with a small wheeled suitcase.\n00:06:05 · a red leather document folio is visible beneath her left arm.\n00:06:19 · she turns toward the south exit rather than the Belgrade end of the train.\n\nThe face is unobstructed and matches Elena’s passport photograph. The folio has the same brass corner and diagonal scuff listed in Damjan’s luggage inventory.",
 "evidence:evidence.platform_image.name": "The Skopje platform image",
 "evidence:evidence.platform_image.summary": "At 00:06, Elena leaves through the rear sleeper door carrying a small suitcase and Damjan’s red folio.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_report.detail": "Preliminary report by Inspector Stefan Jovic, Preševo rail border post, filed 02:38 on Saturday 13 November 2027.\n\nVictim: Damjan Ristev, 52, claims investigator.\nLocation: lower berth, Compartment 6, sleeping car 218.\nEstimated death: 00:10–00:35, subject to full examination.\nCause: internal bleeding from a single narrow puncture beneath the left shoulder. The injury would not necessarily cause immediate collapse.\n\nThe sliding door was closed and its privacy bolt was engaged from inside. Officers used the external emergency release, bending the bolt socket. The night window was latched. No weapon was found. Damjan’s wallet, watch and passport were present; a red document folio listed on his luggage card was not.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_report.name": "The border police report",
 "evidence:evidence.police_report.summary": "Damjan Ristev was found dead in Compartment 6, which was genuinely bolted from inside.",
 "evidence:evidence.sealed_report.detail": "A report sealed in a blue sleeping-car ticket envelope and addressed to the Belgrade Civil Inquiry.\n\nDamjan writes that the 2011 fire investigation identified a body from its berth and luggage before medical records arrived. A later archive comparison suggests that the woman listed as the survivor may actually have been the sister listed as dead. He asks the inquiry to compare the original berth manifest, post-mortem dental chart and the sisters’ separate treatment records.\n\nThe final section concerns a foundation transfer made before the fire. Damjan writes: ‘If the identity is reversed, the transfer was not committed by a dead woman. The person who benefited has been signing the victim’s name ever since.’",
 "evidence:evidence.sealed_report.name": "Damjan’s sealed inquiry report",
 "evidence:evidence.sealed_report.summary": "Damjan hid the original report behind the berth and warned that the 2011 survivor may have been recorded under the wrong sister’s name.",
 "evidence:evidence.vestibule_blood.detail": "One round drop of Damjan’s blood sits in the protected groove of the rear platform threshold. A longer left-hand smear marks the corridor-side rail at shoulder height. Both are older than the damp air deposited after the train left Skopje.\n\nA short grey wool fibre is caught under the steel rail bracket. It does not match Damjan’s dark coat. The blood placement is consistent with Damjan turning away from the platform door, steadying himself with his left hand and entering the sleeper corridor.",
 "evidence:evidence.vestibule_blood.name": "Blood in the rear vestibule",
 "evidence:evidence.vestibule_blood.summary": "Damjan’s blood begins beside the Skopje platform door and transfers to the handrail leading into the corridor.",
 "suspects:suspects.elena.bio": "Elena survived the 2011 Demir Kapija sleeper fire that killed her younger sister Mila. She later rebuilt the Danevski Relief Foundation and became one of its most recognisable public faces. Damjan asked to speak with her before Skopje. Elena says the conversation was brief, the accusations were cruel and she left the train before midnight because she felt unwell.",
 "suspects:suspects.elena.dismissal": "Surviving an old fire does not make me responsible for a new death.",
 "suspects:suspects.elena.name": "Elena Danevska",
 "suspects:suspects.elena.rebuttal": "Damjan wanted to turn the worst night of my life into a public spectacle. I left because I could not breathe in that carriage, not because I killed him.",
 "suspects:suspects.elena.role": "The foundation director",
 "suspects:suspects.emil.bio": "Emil controls the berth cards, passport rack, luggage slips and emergency release for sleeping car 218. He found Damjan at Preševo after the compartment call went unanswered. Emil insists that every early departure was written on the manifest and that nobody could have opened Compartment 6 without leaving a mark on his key register.",
 "suspects:suspects.emil.dismissal": "A bad manifest makes me careless, not violent.",
 "suspects:suspects.emil.name": "Emil Stojanov",
 "suspects:suspects.emil.rebuttal": "I was working the forward door while Skopje unloaded the train. I lied about one passenger leaving early because I took money. I did not go near the rear vestibule with Damjan.",
 "suspects:suspects.emil.role": "The sleeper attendant",
 "suspects:suspects.hana.bio": "Hana was the junior forensic dentist assigned to the burned sleeper in 2011. Her signature appears on the provisional identification, although the original dental records arrived after the case was closed. Damjan asked her to make a new comparison for the Belgrade inquiry. If the first identification was careless, her professional reputation will carry the damage.",
 "suspects:suspects.hana.dismissal": "A mistaken form sixteen years ago is not evidence of murder tonight.",
 "suspects:suspects.hana.name": "Dr. Hana Koleva",
 "suspects:suspects.hana.rebuttal": "I had every reason to fear Damjan’s report and every reason to finish it correctly. I was in the dining car when he went to the rear vestibule.",
 "suspects:suspects.hana.role": "The forensic odontologist",
 "suspects:suspects.mara.bio": "Mara writes long investigations about public money and forgotten court cases. She claims that sharing Train 417 with Damjan was useful coincidence, but her notebook is already organised around the Demir Kapija fire and the Danevski foundation. A Sunday publication deadline would make Damjan’s missing report extremely valuable to her.",
 "suspects:suspects.mara.dismissal": "Wanting the truth before another newspaper is not a murder motive.",
 "suspects:suspects.mara.name": "Mara Petreska",
 "suspects:suspects.mara.rebuttal": "I paid for research and hid it because confidential work is easy to misrepresent. Hana sat across from me until the Skopje departure call.",
 "suspects:suspects.mara.role": "The investigative journalist",
 "suspects:suspects.nikola.bio": "Nikola manages the foundation’s buildings and finances. He identified the sisters’ luggage after the 2011 fire and signed the family insurance settlement the following year. His ticket ended at Kumanovo, where a platform gate recorded his exit at 00:44. He says Damjan was reopening grief for the sake of a report nobody needed.",
 "suspects:suspects.nikola.dismissal": "Protecting my family is not the same as killing for it.",
 "suspects:suspects.nikola.name": "Nikola Danevski",
 "suspects:suspects.nikola.rebuttal": "I argued with Damjan because he spoke about my sisters as entries in a ledger. I left at the station printed on my ticket, in front of cameras and railway staff.",
 "suspects:suspects.nikola.role": "The sisters’ brother",
 "suspects:suspects.petar.bio": "Petar works in the railway’s paper archive and knows the old sleeper-car mechanisms better than most current crews. His father was the attendant blamed for delaying the 2011 evacuation. Petar found the unopened dental envelope that persuaded Damjan to reopen the case, but he feared Damjan’s report would correct the names without clearing his father.",
 "suspects:suspects.petar.dismissal": "Knowing how a sleeper door works does not put me behind one.",
 "suspects:suspects.petar.name": "Petar Rusev",
 "suspects:suspects.petar.rebuttal": "I wanted Damjan to finish the report. I wanted my father’s name in it. Killing him would leave both histories unfinished.",
 "suspects:suspects.petar.role": "The railway archivist"
}
